     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Thanks Huidong, but I don&#39;t quite see how this works in my application. I&#39;ll be a bit more specific. Say I have a function which eventually calls runApp(). E.g.,<div><br></div><div>myfun &lt;- function(){</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>  # do some stuff</div><div><br></div><div>  #run the app</div><div>  runApp(ui = ...., server = ...)</div><div>  </div><div>  return(something_defined_globally)</div><div><br></div><div>}</div><div><br>\r\n</div><div>The problem is that if the application closes early the last return() statement is never called. I&#39;d at least like to return something from this call if runApp() stopes early, but I&#39;m not sure how exactly to use the session$onEnded declarations you mentioned following the early runApp() closing before stopApp() is called. Any tips on what to do here?</div>\r\n<div><br></div><div>Phil</div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
